Z||000000||The Fieromaster||07-15-2001||12:54 AM||||I swapped the engine from myold 85GT into my 85GT fastback... but i am having the same fuel pump problem i did on the old 85 gt..  damn thing wont run with ignition!!  Last time i just ran a manual pump switch... this time id like to do it right... I tried replacing relay,, no go..  If all else fails ill just run a manual switch again BUT what wire leaving the tank harness do i connect the 12v power to?? what color is the wire?? I cant remember and dont want to smoke my gauge sending unit guessing... any help?? please!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||07-15-2001||01:58 AM||||Sounds like you transplanted the problem, along with the engine. I'm guessing it's the oil pressure switch. Not sure which sensor it is. There are a couple for oil pressue.<BR>Is the harness the one that was originally in the car, or did it get transplanted in with the engine? If it came in with the engine, it could be the harness, too. Not sure about wire colors. I have an 88 shop manual. Don't know if 85 is the same or not.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||07-15-2001||10:44 AM||||yea thats the problem i think... transplanted the problem, because the harness on the engine is one that was on engine not the on from the car...  I think it may be the harness.  I think im just gonna run a manual switch...  But i still dont know which wire is the one that needs power.<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000003||dgroves||07-15-2001||12:39 PM||||Having same problem with my '86GT. Fuel pump relay won't energize when the ignition is turned on.(It's suposed to run for a couple of seconds when the ign. is turned on.) I put a volt/ohm meter on the leads to the relay coil and it shows 12v but less than 200mA. Show's this reading all the time, not just the two seconds. Tried the same test at the ECM and got the same results. I think my problem is the fuel pump driver in the ECM has fried. I'm gonna try and find another ECM to see if this problem goes away. Does anybody have a better idea or suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||07-15-2001||12:42 PM||||Well seeing as the ECM in my car is the same as its always been and it was ok when i had the origanal engine in it but the problem was transplanted when i put the other engine and harness in i determinmed it must be my harness!?!?!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||07-15-2001||12:46 PM||||Hey guys,<BR>There is a single wire in the battery/water pump area that has to be plugged in for the fuel pump to work.  it is a one wire connector, I think it stick out of the loom going from the body connector to the engine.<P>Make sure it is connected...otherwise check the relay.<P>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||dgroves||07-15-2001||01:01 PM||||Me again. The tan & white wire that goes to terminal B at the fuel pump relay is the one that you connect to 12v to run the pump. Also you can connect terminal G of the ALCL to 12V. This will run the pump also.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||07-15-2001||03:23 PM||||Just replace the oil pressure switch or fix the harness. most likely it's the OP switch. It's not that hard to do.<P>It's a far safer and better fix. Last thing you want in a wreck is the fuel pump locked on with a manual switch. you want that thing killed right along with the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000008||maryjane||07-15-2001||03:24 PM||||ive emailed you the diagram. Haynes'diagrams are not always accurate. use it for what it's worth.<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
